# Known gaps against ito, kept visible on purpose: `<crate> <reason>`. Each line is a migration still to do, not a decision to stay.
ito-testcheck yagura keeps TESTING.md itself as the checklist (lane scripts and tests/checklist.rs read its rows); a generated second copy would need the lane scripts reworked first, owner to decide
dirs src/bugreport.rs and src/collect/svc/mac.rs need a home directory; ito-common has none: crate-request uchmk/ito#8
postcard src/remote/proto.rs is already the ito-ipc frame on the wire but needs encode-once, read_body and head helpers: crate-request uchmk/ito#9
